{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user's task is to implement `cmd/nproc/main.go` for task #5188 in the go-unix-utils project. This is a stitch task from a code generation pipeline. The nproc utility prints the number of available processing units to stdout. The implementation must cover SRD srd046-nproc requirements R1.1-R1.4:\n   - R1.1: Print available processing units count with no arguments, exit 0\n   - R1.2: `--all` flag prints installed processor count\n   - R1.3: `--ignore=N` subtracts N from count, minimum result is 1\n   - R1.4: Output terminated with trailing newline\n   - Additionally, R1.4 from SRD: `--all` and `--ignore=N` can be combined (ignore subtracts from installed count)\n   \n   Design decision D1: Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go Unix utility reimplementation verified via differential testing against GNU reference binaries\n   - `runtime.NumCPU()` for getting processor count in Go\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Flag parsing for `--all` (boolean) and `--ignore=N` (integer)\n   - On macOS, available and installed CPU counts may be identical (no cgroup support)\n   - Copyright header required: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max\n   - No git commands allowed (orchestrator manages git)\n   - Build with `go build -o bin/nproc ./cmd/nproc/`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd046-nproc.yaml` (READ)\n      - Full SRD for nproc, confirms requirements R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.3 (error handling), R3.1-R3.3 (differential testing)\n      - Non-goals: no CPU affinity, no cgroup limits on macOS\n      - Key detail: `--ignore=N` result must never be less than 1\n      - Key detail: `--all` and `--ignore=N` can be combined, ignore subtracts from installed count\n   \n   - `cmd/nproc/main.go` (TO BE CREATED)\n      - The sole file to create for this task\n      - Must implement nproc utility with --all and --ignore=N flags\n   \n   - `pkg/sys/` source code provided inline in project_context:\n      - `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - must be called at start of main\n      - `sigpipe.go` and `signal.go` contain the implementation\n   \n   - `pkg/testutils/` contract provided:\n      - `BuildBinary(t, \".\")`, `RunDiffTests()`, `DiffTest` struct\n      - Reference binary: `gnproc` via `exec.LookPath`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - implementation has not started.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand full requirements before implementation\n   - Identified that on macOS, `runtime.NumCPU()` returns the same value for both available and installed counts (no cgroup/affinity distinction)\n   - The task scope is R1.1-R1.4 only (core implementation), not R2 (error handling) or R3 (differential testing), though basic error handling for unknown flags should still work via Go's flag package\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive task prompt with full project context, SRDs, source code, architecture, constitutions, and detailed task description for implementing cmd/nproc/main.go (task #5188)\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/nproc/main.go` with the nproc implementation\n   - Verify with `go build -o bin/nproc ./cmd/nproc/`\n   - Verify with `go vet ./cmd/nproc/`\n   - Test that `bin/nproc` prints a positive integer + newline\n   - Test that `bin/nproc --all` prints total processor count\n   - Test that `bin/nproc --ignore=1` prints one less than default (minimum 1)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd046-nproc.yaml` to understand the full SRD requirements. The next step is to write the `cmd/nproc/main.go` file. The implementation needs:\n   - Copyright header\n   - Package main\n   - Import `fmt`, `os`, `runtime`, `strconv`, `flag` (or manual arg parsing), and `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n   - Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` first\n   - Parse `--all` (bool) and `--ignore=N` (int) flags\n   - Use `runtime.NumCPU()` for both available and installed count (on macOS they're identical)\n   - Apply `--ignore` subtraction with minimum of 1\n   - Print result with `fmt.Println()` (adds trailing newline)\n   - Handle errors: positional args → stderr + exit 1, unknown flags → stderr + exit 1\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/nproc/main.go` with the full implementation, then build and verify. The task description states: \"Implement srd046-nproc R1.1 -- print the number of available processing units to stdout\", \"R1.2 -- --all flag prints total number of installed processors\", \"R1.3 -- --ignore=N flag subtracts N from the count with a minimum result of 1\", \"R1.4 -- output terminated with a trailing newline\". The acceptance criteria require: \"go build -o bin/nproc ./cmd/nproc/ succeeds without errors\" and \"go vet ./cmd/nproc/ reports no issues\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5188/de2710c8-66a4-43d6-bd6a-3c0768face89.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_us